{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would result in inadequate living conditions to prospective occupants on the site, by having insufficient gross internal floor area, which is contrary to the following planning policies: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Technical Housing Standards (Nationally Described Space Standard) (as amended) (DCLG, March 2015); &lt;br&gt;- Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021); &lt;br&gt;- London Plan Guidance: Housing Design Standards (June 2023).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of siting, design and appearance, would create an increased sense of closure. It would also unbalance the symmetry and disrupt the built form of the terrace row and the &#x27;banjo&#x27; and consequently constitute harm to the street scene and the character of the Becontree Estate, which is a non-designated heritage asset. As such, the proposal is contrary to: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2024);&lt;br&gt;- Policies D4 &amp;amp; HC1 of the London Plan (June 2021); &lt;br&gt;- Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD4 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of siting, scale and appearance, would result in detrimental harm to the neighbouring property. Specifically, the proposed development would result in an unacceptable level of noise and disturbance, a material loss of sunlight/daylight, outlook and privacy, and unacceptable overshadowing and overbearing impacts on 29 Joan Road, and a material loss of sunlight/daylight and an unacceptable overshadowing impact on 31a Joan Road, therefore constituting unneighbourly development and contrary to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2024);&lt;br&gt;- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021); &lt;br&gt;- Policies SP2 and DMD1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
